From 5164677a5074b58e50b20ab5d284793eda273d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:52:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] xbt-nta: payee-signed coinbase attestations (inline
 variant), regtest nta@<h>

Research prototype of XBT-NTA (rnd/a1-nta, research/node-template-consensus).
After -testactivationheight=nta@<h> (buried deployment, unscheduled on every
network), ContextualCheckBlock requires every value-bearing coinbase output to
pay a key-path taproot script OP_1 <K>, and each distinct payee (in output order)
to bring a 70-byte OP_RETURN "NTA" 0x02 || sig64: a BIP340 signature by K over
TaggedHash("XBT-NTA/attestation", script || height || nBits || prevhash).
Fits the 83-byte RDTS OP_RETURN limit. Old nodes accept these blocks (soft fork).

Not in this variant: the draft's extra transaction, inclusion list and vtxa
sidecar/P2P. Local only, never pushed (XBT-065).

feature_xbt_nta.py ports the model's test_xbt.py vectors; contrib/xbt-nta has
the 3-node demo (before/after activation, old node follows).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
